1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/release/). It cross-matches the extracted data (which person has which mutations), with the mutation's sift score (how bad it is). Then it performs a few analyses, including plotting.\"\n  source_repository: \"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow\"\n  source_commit: null\n  source_format: \"other\"\n  source_file: \"ares_1kgenome_parallel.sbatch\"\n  schema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n  generated_by: \"gemini\"\n  generated_at: \"2026-03-04T10:00:00Z\"\n  last_modified_at: \"2026-03-04T10:00:00Z\"\nstages:\n  - stage_id: \"stage:individuals_processing\"\n    name: \"Individuals Processing\"\n    order: 1\n    description: \"This stage fetches, parses, and extracts SNP variants for individuals from the 1000 Genomes project data, creating intermediate files per individual and chromosome.\"\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n  - stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    name: \"Merge and Sifting\"\n    order: 2\n    description: \"This stage merges the processed individual data and computes SIFT scores for SNP variants, selecting variants with scores and recording them per chromosome.\"\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n  - stage_id: \"stage:analysis\"\n    name: \"Analysis\"\n    order: 3\n    description: \"This stage measures the overlap in mutations among pairs of individuals by population and chromosome, and calculates the frequency of overlapping mutations.\"\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\ntasks:\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals\"\n    name: \"Individuals\"\n    stage: \"stage:individuals_processing\"\n    executable: \"individuals.py\"\n    description: \"This task fetches and parses the Phase3 data from the 1000 genomes project by chromosome. These files list all of Single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) variants in that chromosome and which individuals have each one. SNPs are the most common type of genetic variation among people, and are the ones we consider in this work. An individual task creates output files for each individual of _rs numbers_ 3, where individuals have mutations on both alleles.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"The task processes a large input VCF file in chunks for each chromosome, generating intermediate tar.gz files for each chunk. It is designed to run multiple instances concurrently, each handling a distinct data segment.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: \"Each instance processes a chunk of a chromosome independently, indicated by a sequence of numbers (j*34) passed as arguments. Many instances run in parallel across multiple nodes.\"\n    io_dominance: \"unknown\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:1000genome_phase3_vcf\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:individuals_raw_chunked_tar\"\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    name: \"Individuals Merge\"\n    stage: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    executable: \"individuals_merge.py\"\n    description: \"This task merges the processed individual SNP data from multiple chunks of a single chromosome, combining them into a single tar archive per chromosome.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads multiple tar.gz files (up to 30 as arguments) from the individuals task for a given chromosome and merges them into a single tar.gz file for that chromosome.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"task_parallel\"\n      description: \"Multiple instances of this task run in parallel, each merging the chunked outputs for a distinct chromosome. Each instance performs a serial merge operation.\"\n    io_dominance: \"unknown\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individuals_raw_chunked_tar\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:individuals_merged_tar\"\n  - task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    name: \"Sifting\"\n    stage: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    executable: \"sifting.py\"\n    description: \"This task computes the SIFT scores of all of the SNPs variants, as computed by the Variant Effect Predictor (VEP). For each chromosome the sifting task processes the corresponding VEP, and selects only the SNPs variants that has a SIFT score, recording in a file (per chromosome) the SIFT score and the SNPs variants ids.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads a VCF file containing annotations for a specific chromosome and processes it to extract and record SIFT scores into a per-chromosome output file.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"task_parallel\"\n      description: \"Multiple instances of this task run in parallel, each processing a distinct chromosome's VEP data.\"\n    io_dominance: \"unknown\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:sifting_vcf_input\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:sift_scores_per_chromosome\"\n  - task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    name: \"Mutation Overlap\"\n    stage: \"stage:analysis\"\n    executable: \"mutation_overlap.py\"\n    description: \"This task measures the overlap in mutations (also called SNPs variants) among pairs of individuals by population and by chromosome.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads merged individual data and SIFT scores for specific chromosome and population combinations to compute mutation overlap results.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: \"Each instance processes a specific chromosome and population combination independently.\"\n    io_dominance: \"unknown\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"output\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individuals_merged_tar\"\n      - \"data:sift_scores_per_chromosome\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_results_per_population_chromosome\"\n  - task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    name: \"Frequency\"\n    stage: \"stage:analysis\"\n    executable: \"frequency.py\"\n    description: \"This task measures the frequency of overlapping in mutations by selecting a number of random individuals, and selecting all SNPs variants without taking into account their SIFT scores.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads merged individual data and raw VCF data for specific chromosome and population combinations to compute mutation frequencies.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: \"Each instance processes a specific chromosome and population combination independently.\"\n    io_dominance: \"unknown\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"output\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individuals_merged_tar\"\n      - \"data:1000genome_phase3_vcf\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:frequency_results_per_population_chromosome\"\ndata_objects: []\npc_edges: []\nworkflow_graph:\n  integrity_hash: null\n  last_generated: null\n  dag_edges: []\n  loop_groups: []\n  critica